<title>ITALY: Fazio urges Italian banks to reduce labour costs.</title>
<headline>Fazio urges Italian banks to reduce labour costs.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central bank governor Antonio Fazio said on Wednesday that Italian banks should cut labour and other costs rapidly to boost profitability.</p>
<p>Fazio told a meeting of the Italian banking association ABI that &quot;some institutions (should) reduce their total personnel spending&quot;.</p>
<p>He said that reduced costs should be accompanied by &quot;measures to boost and diversify income sources&quot;.</p>
<p>The centre-left government reached a preliminary agreement with ABI and unions over job cuts and restructuring in the banking sector earlier this month.</p>
<p>Financial analysts say the sector is heavily overstaffed by comparison with other European countries.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
